WEBVTT

00:01.330 --> 00:02.840
Cut it out!

00:02.980 --> 00:05.460
Stop buying those damn strawberries every single day!

00:05.520 --> 00:08.160
Try putting yourself in my shoes who has to eat all these!

00:08.480 --> 00:12.800
Look! Eating so many strawberries every single day is making my skin silky smooth!

00:12.850 --> 00:17.280
Isn't that good? If you don't want them, why not start by refusing <i>those</i>.

00:17.630 --> 00:19.130
<b>Boxes from left to right:</b> Premium quality, Strawberry King, Gold medal winning

00:23.270 --> 00:27.160
<i>That's right. That night at the Kikukawa Award celebration party,</i>

00:27.520 --> 00:30.370
<i>I happened to run into Usagi-san's elder brother</i>,

00:30.860 --> 00:33.890
<i>and told him that I like strawberries, due to lack of anything to say.</i>

00:34.050 --> 00:35.760
<i>For some reason from that day on,</i>

00:38.720 --> 00:41.060
<i>I've been receiving strawberries every single day.</i>

00:42.050 --> 00:43.650
<i>And Usagi-san, on seeing that,</i>

00:44.710 --> 00:46.790
<i>I don't know what the hell he's competing against--</i>

00:46.910 --> 00:49.510
<i>he buys me strawberry products every single day.</i>

00:50.550 --> 00:53.010
<i>I want to call elder Usagi and ask him to stop,</i>

00:53.610 --> 00:56.760
Customer>             Usami Haruhiko

00:53.610 --> 00:56.760
Invoice no. for inquires

00:54.160 --> 00:56.560
<i>but he didn't write his number on the delivery slip.</i>

00:57.580 --> 00:59.580
<i>And Usagi-san won't tell it to me.</i>

01:00.650 --> 01:02.640
<i>What should I do!?</i>

01:02.960 --> 01:07.960
Third time's a charm

01:08.090 --> 01:13.340
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

01:08.090 --> 01:13.340
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

01:11.740 --> 01:25.010
Junjou Romantica 2

01:13.340 --> 01:16.810
ima futari no story

01:13.340 --> 01:16.810
Now, our story...

01:18.100 --> 01:25.590
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

01:18.100 --> 01:25.590
Our future is going to shine on.

01:29.030 --> 01:34.320
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

01:29.030 --> 01:34.320
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

01:34.790 --> 01:39.150
okubyou ni naru bakari

01:34.790 --> 01:39.150
and always lose my nerve.

01:39.150 --> 01:44.750
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

01:39.150 --> 01:44.750
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

01:44.750 --> 01:48.380
kimi to aeru nara

01:44.750 --> 01:48.380
if it means I can see you.

01:50.410 --> 01:55.390
ame ni utarete furueru koe

01:50.410 --> 01:55.390
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

01:55.720 --> 02:00.990
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

01:55.720 --> 02:00.990
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

02:01.670 --> 02:04.470
boku wa yuku yo

02:01.670 --> 02:04.470
I'll go,

02:04.470 --> 02:11.220
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

02:04.470 --> 02:11.220
Until the day when I can see you.

02:12.040 --> 02:17.230
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

02:12.040 --> 02:17.230
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:17.230 --> 02:20.940
ima futari no story

02:17.230 --> 02:20.940
Now, our story

02:21.100 --> 02:22.750
ugokidashita

02:21.100 --> 02:22.750
has started.

02:22.750 --> 02:27.740
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

02:22.750 --> 02:27.740
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

02:27.740 --> 02:34.930
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

02:27.740 --> 02:34.930
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

02:38.980 --> 02:42.080
Thanks for the strawberries yesterday. They were delicious!

02:42.420 --> 02:45.010
The ones that come in wooden boxes sure are something else.

02:46.000 --> 02:46.940
Great!

02:46.990 --> 02:49.570
Sumi-senpai, please take some more with you today too.

02:49.840 --> 02:51.170
I have some cake too.

02:51.780 --> 02:55.540
What? You still have the strawberry fair going on?

02:56.170 --> 03:00.370
I'd really like to shut it down more than anything, but there are some complications...

03:00.980 --> 03:03.430
Hey! Want some cake?

03:03.670 --> 03:05.960
Eh!? Really? Nice!

03:05.950 --> 03:09.800
Oh yeah, seems like the Kikukawa Award party was pretty amazing, huh?

03:10.120 --> 03:14.120
I heard he was surrounded by all these screaming girls, like a famous actor or something.

03:14.740 --> 03:16.670
Eh? Why do you know that?

03:17.720 --> 03:19.980
That's what it said in some magazine.

03:20.210 --> 03:20.870
Oh...

03:21.540 --> 03:26.930
For someone who hates Usagi-san, you sure keep a follow up of him, right?

03:28.800 --> 03:30.340
What are you trying to say?

03:30.900 --> 03:31.360
Eh...

03:31.930 --> 03:34.730
In truth, I like Usagi-san or something...?

03:35.190 --> 03:37.620
No, no! That's not what I...

03:42.910 --> 03:45.910
Don't worry. The one I like is Misaki.

03:46.070 --> 03:47.800
No, no, no. No need.

03:47.800 --> 03:51.550
I just want to live my life as a normal male college student!

03:51.910 --> 03:56.240
Oh... speaking of which, do you have any plans for the school festival?

03:57.120 --> 03:58.130
Huh? No.

03:58.180 --> 04:00.730
I was thinking that I'd just work my part-time job that day.

04:01.090 --> 04:03.200
If you don't mind, I could really use your help.

04:03.790 --> 04:04.620
Okay.

04:05.300 --> 04:07.250
Your circle is...?

04:07.280 --> 04:11.040
Mitsuhashi University, Onsen Research Group. In short, ORG.

04:11.280 --> 04:14.430
We're putting up a traditional haunted house.

04:15.680 --> 04:18.090
Ah, speaking of "Onsen" one thinks of "hot spring steam."

04:18.280 --> 04:19.690
Speaking of "hot spring steam" one thinks of...

04:19.690 --> 04:21.810
That's right! Murder cases!

04:22.840 --> 04:25.800
Throw in some femme fatale, maybe some gourmet cuisine,

04:25.800 --> 04:28.580
and one of those traditional old fashioned towns for the settings and it's perfect!

04:28.640 --> 04:29.650
Yes, yes.

04:30.890 --> 04:31.940
I'll do it!

04:32.080 --> 04:34.830
I may not look it but I love suspense!

04:34.900 --> 04:36.800
I also watch lots of such drama!

04:37.090 --> 04:43.460
Old town mystery, steamy onsen and delicious food, murder in a mixed bath, a casual journey of exploration and discovery!

04:44.770 --> 04:46.420
But it's a haunted house.

04:48.550 --> 04:52.720
<i>School festival! I am feeling like a normal college student now. </i>

04:54.320 --> 04:57.360
<i>Oh crap! Battery's about to run out.</i>

04:58.310 --> 05:03.260
<i>Ever since I started living at Usagi-san's place, the extraordinary has become the ordinary...</i>

05:03.680 --> 05:07.100
<i>Not good. If that's considering something as normal, it's bad for a person.</i>

05:09.560 --> 05:14.250
<i>Besides, it just doesn't make sense for one man to have so much bizarre-ness all over the place.</i>

05:15.250 --> 05:16.930
<i>Those sort of things are...</i>

05:17.720 --> 05:19.840
Standing right here!!

05:21.620 --> 05:22.800
Wait a moment.

05:23.210 --> 05:24.800
<i>Ugh...! What?</i>

05:25.130 --> 05:27.300
<i>Why do I have to run into him here!?</i>

05:27.650 --> 05:31.770
I didn't think I'd actually see you if I just drove by here, but...

05:33.090 --> 05:34.860
Destiny is what they call this, right?

05:35.860 --> 05:37.650
No, that is...

05:38.160 --> 05:39.030
<i>This guy...</i>

05:40.400 --> 05:43.750
<i>His face or voice is nothing like Usagi-san, but</i>

05:44.760 --> 05:46.720
<i>they're exactly the same at heart, is what I think.</i>

05:47.270 --> 05:49.440
Are the strawberries getting delivered to you properly?

05:49.700 --> 05:53.200
<i>Oh, that's right! Now that we've met here, it's a good chance for me to ask him to stop!</i>

05:53.600 --> 05:56.360
U-Um, Thank you very much!

05:56.850 --> 05:59.790
I'm very grateful for your kindness, but that's enough.

06:00.350 --> 06:02.350
Did something displease you?

06:02.740 --> 06:07.040
Eh, oh no, that's not it... so, umm...

06:08.220 --> 06:11.190
Receiving them day after day is a bad idea.

06:11.260 --> 06:13.420
Then should I send them every other day?

06:13.620 --> 06:15.760
No! That's not what I meant...

06:15.760 --> 06:17.560
What's the harm?

06:17.610 --> 06:19.390
I mean that...!

06:19.130 --> 06:21.390
What? What's happening? A quarrel?

06:24.980 --> 06:28.570
W-Wait! Let go of me! What are you doing!?

06:28.900 --> 06:30.800
We'll continue the rest at home.

06:30.990 --> 06:33.060
I want to hear a proper reason.

06:33.550 --> 06:35.150
What!? No!

06:35.180 --> 06:38.370
It's just a talk about me requesting you to not send the strawberries anymore!

06:38.610 --> 06:40.550
Why do I have to go for such a reason?

06:41.520 --> 06:44.970
Huh? "Home" meaning Usagi-san's family home?

06:47.530 --> 06:50.160
We're attracting attention. Hurry and get inside.

06:50.900 --> 06:52.290
<i>W-What should I do?</i>

06:53.130 --> 06:55.380
<i>I'm just a bit... curious.</i>

07:04.290 --> 07:05.720
Hey! Misaki!...

07:09.040 --> 07:09.740
Misaki...

07:24.430 --> 07:25.350
<i>Japan...?</i>

07:27.150 --> 07:28.540
What are you doing?

07:28.790 --> 07:29.970
Ah... No...

07:31.080 --> 07:35.470
There's like 100 meters between the gate and the front door...

07:36.810 --> 07:41.220
<i>I mean, I knew they were rich, but to this extent is...!</i>

07:43.100 --> 07:46.030
<i>Seriously, is this really in central Tokyo!?</i>

07:47.010 --> 07:48.360
Welcome back.

07:48.690 --> 07:49.520
Maid!?

07:50.100 --> 07:51.790
Huh? Alexander!?

07:52.360 --> 07:53.280
T-Tama!?

07:53.330 --> 07:54.390
Why do you know?

07:54.610 --> 07:55.400
<i>Seriously!?</i>

07:58.720 --> 08:00.890
Haruhiko-sama, welcome back.

08:01.830 --> 08:03.400
Do we have a guest?

08:03.820 --> 08:04.320
Yes.

08:08.460 --> 08:09.640
Welcome.

08:09.830 --> 08:12.330
I'm the butler of this house.

08:12.600 --> 08:14.510
<i>Butler! Speaking of butler...</i>

08:14.560 --> 08:15.500
Sebastian!

08:16.170 --> 08:17.740
My name is Tanaka.

08:18.110 --> 08:18.890
Oh...

08:31.000 --> 08:35.570
<i>No matter how I think, I'm obviously out of place as a guest here...</i>

08:36.100 --> 08:43.970
<i>But this house... maybe it's because it's so huge, but it feels kind of cold.</i>

08:50.030 --> 08:51.700
I'm very sorry.

08:52.210 --> 08:56.190
Haruhiko-sama wishes to tell you that he is occupied with work and will be a little late.

08:57.420 --> 08:59.070
Please wait a bit longer.

08:59.290 --> 09:01.240
A-Ah, yes. It's fine.

09:03.740 --> 09:06.700
U-Um, this is an amazing house!

09:07.010 --> 09:09.480
Apparently, it was built around the middle of the Meiji era.

09:12.010 --> 09:17.580
It's very rare for Haruhiko-sama to bring a guest like you to the house...

09:18.220 --> 09:21.630
Please excuse me, but are you a business acquaintance?

09:22.240 --> 09:28.800
Oh no, I'm currently staying at Usa-, err... Akihiko-san's home right now.

09:31.200 --> 09:37.120
Umm, my brother and Akihiko-san were classmates in highschool, that's how it happened.

09:39.920 --> 09:41.560
<i>That reaction again...</i>

09:42.560 --> 09:45.620
Um, I've received a lot of help from Akihiko-san.

09:45.990 --> 09:48.860
O-Oh, no, excuse me.

09:49.300 --> 09:55.640
Akihiko-sama wasn't really the kind of person who'd do something like that, so I was just a bit surprised.

09:56.030 --> 09:56.530
<i>Eh?</i>

09:58.640 --> 10:00.720
Is he well?

10:01.190 --> 10:02.710
Oh, yes.

10:04.160 --> 10:08.620
Even in his childhood, he always kept his distance from home.

10:08.880 --> 10:12.240
After graduating from high school he immediately left the house.

10:13.080 --> 10:15.060
Didn't he have any friends?

10:16.580 --> 10:20.320
In the house across from here, there was a boy about his age.

10:20.730 --> 10:23.670
They were very good friends.

10:25.730 --> 10:28.800
But when he'd return home, he'd say very little.

10:29.350 --> 10:31.400
There is a storeroom on the second floor.

10:31.500 --> 10:36.300
He would often sit there looking outside the window, writing something.

10:39.040 --> 10:41.330
Oh, he's well now.

10:42.130 --> 10:45.800
Though he does tend to keep an irregular schedule due to his work.

10:47.170 --> 10:49.800
I make all the meals now.

10:50.330 --> 10:53.610
Except green peas, he's eating everything properly.

10:54.060 --> 10:55.440
Is that so.

10:55.940 --> 11:00.410
Then it means that Akihiko-sama must have opened up his heart to you.

11:01.060 --> 11:03.320
Eh!? I don't know...

11:03.530 --> 11:04.880
...maybe a little...

11:05.590 --> 11:06.680
That's good.

11:07.710 --> 11:10.870
So did you meet Haruhiko-sama through Akihiko-sama?

11:11.300 --> 11:13.870
Ahh, something like that...

11:14.060 --> 11:16.610
But they both don't really look alike.

11:19.330 --> 11:21.050
Do you not know?

11:21.650 --> 11:23.360
Huh? About what?

11:23.810 --> 11:29.540
O-Oh no, it's really too bold of me to say this, but...

11:33.080 --> 11:38.270
That is... they don't have much contact with each other... that is...

11:38.270 --> 11:41.100
Oh... yes, I know about that.

11:42.690 --> 11:46.850
The truth is, they were born to different mothers...

11:47.430 --> 11:48.150
Sorry!?

11:50.100 --> 11:51.030
<i>That means...</i>

11:52.700 --> 11:54.380
What were you talking about?

11:55.050 --> 11:56.720
Remember your place.

11:58.920 --> 12:00.340
Please excuse me.

12:03.820 --> 12:09.840
<i>So then, that means Usagi-san and Usagi elder are half-brothers?</i>

12:10.560 --> 12:11.460
What is it?

12:11.700 --> 12:14.040
Did he say anything unecessary?

12:14.240 --> 12:15.630
No, nothing.

12:18.050 --> 12:19.050
<i>That's right!</i>

12:19.270 --> 12:20.640
<i>Right now, rather than anything else...</i>

12:20.770 --> 12:24.200
Um, so about the strawberries...

12:24.250 --> 12:27.520
That's enough! They were very delicious though.

12:27.840 --> 12:30.340
If they are delicious, there's no reason to refuse them.

12:30.480 --> 12:32.410
No, well about that...

12:32.480 --> 12:34.770
Then is there anything else that you like?

12:34.970 --> 12:41.020
Ahh, that's right, I guess if I had to say, maybe cherries...

12:41.020 --> 12:42.090
Cherries.

12:44.340 --> 12:45.240
Understood.

12:45.350 --> 12:48.900
Ah! No, that's not it! Not cherries!

12:48.950 --> 12:51.550
I just picked something randomly!

12:51.590 --> 12:55.540
Ah, um, seriously, it's enough! Really!!

12:55.950 --> 12:57.680
Hey, are you listening!?

12:58.080 --> 13:01.350
I had a bit of research done about you.

13:01.470 --> 13:05.000
About your current situation and your environment.

13:05.690 --> 13:06.500
What?

13:08.180 --> 13:09.170
Come in.

13:09.920 --> 13:11.730
I prepared this for you.

13:11.780 --> 13:12.260
Huh?

13:12.510 --> 13:15.180
Leave Akihiko's home and live here.

13:16.210 --> 13:19.740
It's only 10 minutes to Mitsuhashi University from here by train.

13:19.970 --> 13:23.070
I don't mind arranging a car for you too, if you want.

13:23.680 --> 13:26.410
W-What are you saying so suddenly!?

13:27.090 --> 13:31.360
Even if it's working out right now, living together with him is bound to get difficult at some point.

13:32.920 --> 13:34.120
<i>What does that mean?</i>

13:34.640 --> 13:37.960
<i>That if I'm here, it'd cause trouble for Usagi-san?</i>

13:39.580 --> 13:41.150
That's none of your business.

13:41.340 --> 13:45.220
Even if something did happen, I could always go to my brother's place.

13:46.300 --> 13:50.900
Because there were problem of staying with your brother, you went to <i>his</i> place, right?

13:52.170 --> 13:55.600
In that case, I could just live on my own.

13:56.190 --> 13:58.990
I already know you that can't afford that.

13:59.800 --> 14:01.770
That's none of your business!

14:02.020 --> 14:04.100
Don't go investigating other people on your own whim.

14:04.420 --> 14:05.240
I'm going home.

14:07.570 --> 14:08.300
What?

14:08.950 --> 14:11.880
All your problems could get solved if you stayed here.

14:12.430 --> 14:15.670
It'd be much more comfortable living here than at Akihiko's home.

14:16.660 --> 14:19.520
Why do I have the need for any of that?

14:20.420 --> 14:22.440
I believe I've already told you that I love you.

14:22.710 --> 14:25.840
U-Uh, that's the thing, it's just strange!

14:26.200 --> 14:28.670
I didn't particularly do anything for you.

14:28.730 --> 14:30.420
Why does it have to be me?

14:32.210 --> 14:33.190
That is...

14:38.710 --> 14:41.420
Haruhiko-sama, there's a call for you.

14:41.600 --> 14:43.610
Hang up. I'll call them later.

14:43.860 --> 14:45.020
About that...

14:45.470 --> 14:48.250
...-sama on the line ...insists on speaking with you...

14:48.250 --> 14:50.010
I understand. I'll come now.

14:52.360 --> 14:53.340
Come with me.

14:53.870 --> 14:57.000
E-Eh, wait, what? Let go of me!

15:00.520 --> 15:01.160
Wai-

15:02.580 --> 15:03.370
Eh!?

15:04.400 --> 15:07.270
Wai-Wait a  minute! Hey! Open up!!

15:07.640 --> 15:11.210
I have no intention of harming you. Just wait there for a few minutes.

15:11.920 --> 15:15.500
What!? Stop kidding me! What's the meaning of this!?

15:15.610 --> 15:18.880
Open up! Hey! Wait! Seriously, open up!!

15:22.250 --> 15:23.780
Tanaka-san!

15:23.920 --> 15:26.140
Ta-na-ka-san!

15:28.400 --> 15:29.700
This is bad.

15:29.740 --> 15:31.590
Ahh, phone, phone!

15:32.630 --> 15:33.670
<b>Please recharge</b>

15:34.020 --> 15:36.880
AHHH!! It's useless!!

15:39.160 --> 15:40.210
That's it!

15:44.820 --> 15:50.080
Excuse me!! Is somebody there!?

15:50.080 --> 15:52.250
...somebody there!?

15:54.650 --> 15:58.150
Is this really Japan!?

15:59.420 --> 16:00.350
What should I do?

16:00.480 --> 16:02.930
In this situation, I'll have break down the door by force.

16:04.440 --> 16:05.820
Is there something here I can use?

16:08.200 --> 16:09.050
A notebook?

16:13.180 --> 16:17.120
<b>Usami Akihiko
May 2nd</b>

16:14.400 --> 16:16.650
Oh, this is Usagi-san's...

16:18.720 --> 16:22.400
So this is the storeroom Tanaka-san was talking about?

16:24.460 --> 16:26.130
Usagi-san... here...

16:33.010 --> 16:34.340
Akihiko-sama!

16:35.240 --> 16:36.740
Is he here?

16:37.200 --> 16:40.890
He would have brought him along, a boy looking like a high school student.

16:41.180 --> 16:43.390
Yes, certainly he looked like that.

16:43.500 --> 16:45.010
He already left.

16:46.400 --> 16:47.550
What's this about?

16:48.790 --> 16:50.810
I saw you both near the University.

16:51.100 --> 16:52.920
I can't reach him on his phone,

16:55.100 --> 16:57.720
and he wasn't in any of the places I checked.

16:58.360 --> 17:00.310
So I figured this was the only place he could be.

17:00.610 --> 17:03.700
Too bad. You just missed him.

17:04.770 --> 17:07.760
Like always, you're upto your good-for-nothing tricks.

17:08.700 --> 17:11.340
You finally bother to come home, only to make accusations?

17:11.370 --> 17:14.240
Looks like novelists have quiet a bit of free time on their hands.

17:24.750 --> 17:25.780
What's the matter?

17:25.860 --> 17:28.470
I wonder. He's usually quiet well behaved.

17:42.170 --> 17:44.900
Awesome! I feel kind of cool!

17:45.010 --> 17:48.130
Seems like an escape scene from a comic book or a movie!

17:52.060 --> 17:52.820
Misaki!

17:53.760 --> 17:54.290
Eh?

17:55.790 --> 17:56.440
What!?

17:57.800 --> 17:59.000
Misaki!!

18:01.230 --> 18:03.470
This is terrible! Quickly call the doctor!

18:03.590 --> 18:04.640
Yes!

18:06.760 --> 18:08.560
Hey! Misaki! Misaki!

18:08.760 --> 18:10.260
Hey! Get a grip!

18:12.470 --> 18:14.190
I'm alright...

18:15.070 --> 18:16.770
Hadn't he gone home?

18:23.050 --> 18:26.320
I believe I've been quiet no matter what you stole from me before.

18:27.160 --> 18:28.990
But I won't stay quiet when it comes to him.

18:29.750 --> 18:31.830
Don't make me seriously angry.

18:32.950 --> 18:34.140
What does that mean?

18:35.320 --> 18:36.650
It means this.

18:45.580 --> 18:47.280
Bastard, what are you suddenly...!?

18:49.060 --> 18:49.790
We're leaving.

18:50.000 --> 18:52.760
Wai-! Put me down! Put me down!

18:52.960 --> 18:53.730
Usagi-sa-

18:53.460 --> 18:56.800
Akihiko-sama, the doctor will be here in just a moment!

18:57.920 --> 18:58.890
No need.

18:59.120 --> 19:00.890
Put me down already!

19:02.720 --> 19:03.740
Akihiko...

19:07.430 --> 19:11.030
S-Stop it, Usagi-san! It's the parking garage.

19:11.440 --> 19:13.600
What if someone from the mansion saw us!?

19:13.650 --> 19:14.850
Let them see.

19:15.290 --> 19:18.120
Are you stupid!? I don't have such a hobby!

19:18.170 --> 19:20.970
Stop it already! I'm injured!

19:21.120 --> 19:23.160
Consider getting away with just a sprain a miracle!

19:23.550 --> 19:25.280
Half of it was your damn fault!

19:26.240 --> 19:29.470
Aren't you the one you told me to make him stop sending the strawberries?

19:29.840 --> 19:32.160
Does that imply that you can cheerfully follow him?

19:32.310 --> 19:33.780
You're too careless!

19:34.220 --> 19:35.740
Hey! What's this?

19:35.870 --> 19:39.680
Are you trying to say that you would be lonely if I wasn't around?

19:42.360 --> 19:44.180
Idiot! What are you doing!?

19:49.810 --> 19:51.120
I'd be lonely.

19:51.870 --> 19:53.280
W-What's with that?

19:54.100 --> 19:57.020
How would you feel if I wasn't around?

19:57.020 --> 20:00.320
U-Umm, I-I don't know about that...

20:00.640 --> 20:01.940
I won't spare you till you tell me.

20:02.340 --> 20:04.280
I told you I don't know!

20:05.020 --> 20:07.600
I'm no good without you.

20:07.970 --> 20:10.080
W-What's with that!?

20:11.460 --> 20:12.900
Be honest.

20:28.280 --> 20:30.110
A college student getting a piggy back ride...

20:30.340 --> 20:32.160
Would you prefer being carried like a princess?

20:33.040 --> 20:34.470
There's no need for that.

20:37.820 --> 20:45.470
<i>While being locked up in that room, the old notebook that I read through, wasn't a diary but fictional work.</i>

20:46.530 --> 20:49.340
<i>It was full of sad stories...</i>

20:50.620 --> 20:54.140
<i>...but in the end, the main character had his happy ending.</i>

20:55.350 --> 20:58.860
<i>I don't really read many books, so I can't say I understand, but</i>

20:59.360 --> 21:03.330
<i>when Usagi-san wrote this, he might have been feeling lonely.</i>

21:04.440 --> 21:07.050
<i>I want to know more about Usagi-san.</i>

21:07.760 --> 21:08.960
<i>Want to ask him more.</i>

21:10.250 --> 21:12.200
<i>But I can't.</i>

21:12.640 --> 21:16.550
<i>If I do, I feel like I might just bother him.</i>

21:17.300 --> 21:18.160
<i>But you know,</i>

21:18.530 --> 21:22.200
<i>while being locked up, the only thought that kept running desperately through my head was,</i>

21:22.450 --> 21:26.840
<i>"I have to hurry back to Usagi-san's side".</i>

21:39.850 --> 21:44.990
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

21:39.850 --> 21:44.990
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:45.120 --> 21:50.380
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:45.120 --> 21:50.380
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

21:50.730 --> 21:55.750
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

21:50.730 --> 21:55.750
You doubled all my happiness,

21:55.750 --> 22:02.440
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

21:55.750 --> 22:02.440
and halved all my sadness.

22:02.550 --> 22:07.550
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

22:02.550 --> 22:07.550
No matter what path I walk in the future,

22:07.950 --> 22:12.230
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

22:07.950 --> 22:12.230
will surely lead to you.

22:12.230 --> 22:14.990
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

22:12.230 --> 22:14.990
You're there up ahead of me,

22:14.990 --> 22:17.850
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

22:14.990 --> 22:17.850
I'm there ahead of you,

22:17.850 --> 22:23.120
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

22:17.850 --> 22:23.120
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

22:23.120 --> 22:29.020
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

22:23.120 --> 22:29.020
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

22:29.610 --> 22:34.090
mou doko he mo ikanaide

22:29.610 --> 22:34.090
Hey, don't go anywhere.

22:34.090 --> 22:39.550
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

22:34.090 --> 22:39.550
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:39.550 --> 22:44.940
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:39.550 --> 22:44.940
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:44.940 --> 22:50.760
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:44.940 --> 22:50.760
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

22:51.150 --> 22:56.440
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

22:51.150 --> 22:56.440
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

22:59.940 --> 23:03.860
Oh, Sumi-senpai, I've got cherries. They're amazing!

23:03.950 --> 23:07.500
They don't call them rubies of the fruit world for nothing! They're something else!

23:08.200 --> 23:11.200
Oh... Sorry. I don't like cherries.

23:11.500 --> 23:13.540
Huh!? But why!?

23:13.400 --> 23:19.940
<b>Note:</b> Usami is shopping for premium cherries.

23:14.030 --> 23:15.090
About that...

23:15.440 --> 23:20.340
I always thought that having that big a pit in a fruit that size was kind of weird.

23:20.490 --> 23:24.020
L-Let's eat them! They're really delicious!

23:24.200 --> 23:28.700
My brother and his wife are on a vacation right now, you're the only one I can rely on!

23:28.940 --> 23:29.720
Nope, I can't.

23:29.720 --> 23:33.250
I'm begging you! Please!

23:30.160 --> 23:31.820
Takahashi Misaki, 19 years old.

23:31.890 --> 23:34.160
The Cherry Offensive has begun!

23:35.510 --> 23:46.090
